/* GeoFlock: many creatures on the tour stops about a biome, an ecosystem or a wildlife habitat (the user's request: "we
   should label the amazon with lots of animals. same elsewhere in animal related tours. if there is a stop on a biome or
   ecosystem or anything, try to find lots of creatures and point to the map").
   - Photo pins: animals that really live there, each at a real place inside the habitat (the shape of the other photo
     pins: {at:[lon,lat],label,col,icon:"photo"}), only up to the tours' five photo pins a stop: the pins already on a stop
     are counted first, and a picture or a name the stop already shows is not used twice. Library photos first; the new
     ones are freely licensed Wikimedia Commons photos (GF_WILD_PHOTOS: author, licence, page), joined to the photo library
     the way geoflock-review-photos2.js does it. Labels are the short captions themselves (at most 20 characters).
   - Then more creatures as small animal symbols through the symbols layer of geoflock-symbols.js (gfSym marks on the
     stop): each one is placed only where it covers no name, pin, photo pin, leader line or card (shifting a few pixels at
     most), otherwise it is left out. That layer knows only its own emoji, so this file gives it the animal pictures: a mark
     here carries e:"gfw_<name>", and the picture is put into the layer's <img> when the layer is built.
     Emoji graphics: Twemoji (CC BY 4.0, by Twitter, Inc. and contributors).
   Nothing is removed or moved: existing stops, texts, pins, labels and symbols stay as they are (a stop that already has
   its own symbols keeps them and gets no new ones). The Geography tour is not touched. geoflock-smallplaces.js stays the
   outermost wrapper (it keeps the photos at a visible distance from their spot); geoflock-pinfix.js is not fought: the
   photos here are not in its list of places.
   Patched by tour id and stop title (zero-width spaces stripped) after window load + 1.5 s, again at +3, +6.5 and +13.5 s
   and on every psGo; fields other patches lock are set with Object.defineProperty (configurable, writable). */
